Arch is rolling release; main URLs can change after this snapshot.
pambase packaging declares GPL-3.0-or-later; openssh packaging has mixed upstream licenses.

OpenSSH prepends Include /etc/ssh/sshd_config.d/*.conf to sshd_config.
99-archlinux.conf supplies KbdInteractiveAuthentication no, UsePAM yes, PrintMotd no.
Installer policy must precede those settings and validate the effective configuration.
Systemd unit is sshd.service, ExecStart=/usr/bin/sshd -D.

Auth traversal is sshd -> system-remote-login -> system-login -> system-auth.
Do not discard system-login's pam_shells/pam_nologin authorization gates.
Preserve system-auth's faillock preauth check and authsucc reset, not its authfail
branch for the removed password credential providers. Retain pam_env policy.
Do not alter account/session/password includes: they preserve pam_access,
pam_nologin, pam_time, pam_limits and other platform policy for key logins too.
Unknown nested custom auth rules must fail closed, not silently disappear.
Systemd-homed credentials are intentionally not accepted as a burner fallback;
its account/session hooks remain, and homed users may require separately managed
home activation. This profile does not claim compatibility with arbitrary Arch derivatives.
